window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-04e32c7389f20958"]={"key":"ny_main-04e32c7389f20958","group":"ny_main","uid":"04e32c7389f20958","rank":65,"title":"wayfinding decision deck blank instrument 01","occupation":"producers_directors","archetype":"artifact_spec","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are Leandra Jankowski, the producer and director responsible for the visitor experience materials at Fernhollow Analytics. Reina Villanueva has asked you to revise the wayfinding presentation for a clinic site after Marlowe Engineering’s annotated floor plans and the visitor-flow workbook disagree about the clear width on the approach to reception. Maren Havlicek needs a decision-ready comparison before the routing choice is approved, and the frozen facilities snapshot is valid only as of 30 September 2025. Use the supplied file `facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx` as the evidence base; it contains the relevant facilities observations, route information, and policy text. Return `elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf` in the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename. It must be a seven-page, 16:9 landscape PDF deck that a senior decision maker can read without specialist training. Compare both routing schemes with coherent diagrams, dimensions, units, and route measures, expose the disagreement rather than smoothing it away, state the source-precedence rule you chose, and recommend one scheme with a concise rationale and the principal trade-off. The deck must explicitly identify the width that falls outside the supplied policy range and show how that condition is accommodated or controlled; do not imply that an out-of-range measurement is compliant merely because another source reports a different value. Include a clearly labelled completion area with an editable field named “Final sign location”; leave that field genuinely blank for later completion, with no guessed location, example, or “TBD” substitute. Keep the user-entry area visibly separate from the read-only calculated comparison so the next person cannot mistake a source value or derived result for an input. Add a compact handoff note explaining what the next user is expected to complete, which snapshot date to verify, and which figures are read-only, but keep the guidance subordinate to the decision content. Render the deck cleanly with no clipped labels, ambiguous units, or diagrams that contradict the comparison. This is needed by 3 October 2025.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx` — Frozen external facilities snapshot containing the workbook measurements, annotated-plan measurements, route segments, visitor-flow observations, supplied width policy, and the unresolved sign-location status used to prepare the deck.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf` — A revised spatial wayfinding decision deck comparing both routing schemes and presenting a bounded recommendation for senior review. (Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Produce exactly seven pages in 16:9 landscape presentation geometry.; Use the supplied facilities snapshot as the sole factual source.; Keep the Final sign location user-entry field blank and distinguish user-entry controls from read-only calculated content.; Include source provenance, the selected precedence rule, both scheme comparisons, the out-of-range-width accommodation, and concise handoff guidance.; The PDF must render without clipping, overlap, unreadable labels, or inconsistent units.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx","bytes":11284,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/21ba1631ebe4170a3d8d787463d4cb1e4a66983e41234b94e1ac3c94504ed65a.xlsx","sha256":"21ba1631ebe4170a3d8d787463d4cb1e4a66983e41234b94e1ac3c94504ed65a","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Snapshot metadata","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Fernhollow Analytics - Facilities Snapshot"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Elmsworth Clinic | frozen reception wayfinding evidence"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Field","Value","Notes"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Snapshot valid through","45930","Do not use for later site changes"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Site","Elmsworth Clinic","Ground-floor public arrival"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Purpose","Reception wayfinding decision","Facilities evidence only"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Evidence role","Visitor-flow workbook","Operational flow and planning observations"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Evidence role","Annotated floor plans","Annotated physical observations"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Measurement basis","Clear width at narrowest point of public reception approach","Use received source units"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Exported","45931.34513888889","Facilities Operations queue"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Request ref","FH-ELM-472",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Measurements","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Reception approach measurements"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Imported facilities observations - values retained as received"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Record ref","routing scheme","Location / approach","Measure","Value as received","Evidence source","Scope","Captured","Reviewer note"]},{"r":"5","cells":["VF-2841","North Loop","Junction to reception","Clear width","1.50 m","Visitor-flow workbook","Public","29 Sep 2025","arrival study"]},{"r":"6","cells":["AP-091","North Loop","Junction to reception","Clear width","1100 mm","Annotated floor plans","Public","30 Sep 2025","markup cloud near desk"]},{"r":"7","cells":["VF-2841","North Loop","Junction to reception","Clear width","1.50 m","Visitor-flow workbook","Public","29 Sep 2025","arrival study"]},{"r":"8","cells":["VF-2849"," south loop ","Corridor to reception","Clear width","1.25 m","visitor flow workbook ","Public","29 Sep 2025","AM queue"]},{"r":"9","cells":["AP-104","SOUTH LOOP","Corridor to reception","Clear width","1450 mm","Annotated Floor Plans","Public","30 Sep 2025","dimension cloud"]},{"r":"10","cells":["AP-105","South Loop","Side return","Clear width","1,O5 m","annotated floor plans","Public","30 Sep 2025","scan text unclear"]},{"r":"11","cells":["LD-031","Loading spur","Staff loading bay","Clear width","2.10 m","Loading schedule","Staff only","28 Sep 2025","not a public approach"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Route segments","row_count":9,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Public route segments"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Route trace lengths used for reception approach comparison"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Route ref","Scheme","Seq.","From","To","Length (m)","Turns recorded","Trace source","Access"]},{"r":"5","cells":["RT-N-01","North Loop","1","Entry","Junction","12","2","Annotated plan route trace","Public"]},{"r":"6","cells":["RT-N-02","North Loop","2","Junction","Reception","19","2","Annotated plan route trace","Public"]},{"r":"7","cells":["RT-S-01","South Loop","1","Entry","Lift lobby","14","3","annotated plan route trace","Public"]},{"r":"8","cells":["RT-S-02","South Loop","2","Lift lobby","Corridor","10","3","annotated plan route trace","Public"]},{"r":"9","cells":["RT-S-03","South Loop","3","Corridor","Reception","12","3","annotated plan route trace","Public"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Flow observations","row_count":7,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Visitor-flow observations"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Arrival-period observations from the visitor-flow workbook"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Flow ref","scheme","Observation window","Visitors","Interval","Evidence source","Access","Comment"]},{"r":"5","cells":["FLOW-778","North Loop","08:30-08:45","18","15 min","Visitor-flow workbook","Public","typical weekday"]},{"r":"6","cells":["FLOW-779","south loop","08:30-08:45","16","15 min","visitor flow workbook","Public","typical weekday"]},{"r":"7","cells":["FLOW-780","Loading spur","08:30-08:45","4","15 min","Service roster","Staff only","deliveries"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Policy and open items","row_count":9,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Policy thresholds and open items"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Public reception approach policy supplied with the facilities snapshot"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Item","Value","Unit","Status","Detail"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Minimum public clear width","1200","mm","Policy","Below 1200 mm is outside the supplied range"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Preferred public clear width","1500","mm","Policy","Preferred target for public approach"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Measurement basis","Narrowest point of public reception approach","","Applies","Clear width only"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Final sign location","","","Unresolved pending later coordination",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Release note","Check snapshot date before approval issue","","Open","No later survey attached"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf","bytes":21715,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/1769bf1cb4bf757019510808757591ad3cf93f94b0ea896ae9134ebd675bfa5b.pdf","sha256":"1769bf1cb4bf757019510808757591ad3cf93f94b0ea896ae9134ebd675bfa5b","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"ELMSWORTH CLINIC | EXECUTIVE REVIEW\n\n\nReception wayfinding decision\n\n\nApprove a clear route to reception                                                                                                                    DECISION NEEDED\n\nTwo public routing schemes reach the same reception point, but the visitor-flow workbook and\nannotated floor plans disagree on the narrow approach width.                                                                                          03 October 2025\n                                                                                                                                                      Approve one public routing scheme\n\n\n\n\n    EVIDENCE WINDOW                                                                      ALTERNATIVES                                             KNOWN CONDITION\n\n\n    30 Sep 2025                                                                          North / South                                            1,100 mm\n    Frozen facilities snapshot valid through this date.                                  Separate public routes; each uses a distinct reception   North Loop plan width is below the 1,200 mm minimum.\n                                                                                         approach.\n\n\n\n\n      DECISION QUESTION\n\n\n      Which route should carry public visitors to reception?\n      This deck separates physical clearance from demand evidence, makes both source values visible, and keeps the unresolved sign-location completion separate from\n      the calculated comparison.\n                                                                                                                                                                       SOURCE: facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                                        1/7\n\fDECISION BASIS\n\n\nEvidence rules and policy frame\n\n\n      SELECTED SOURCE-PRECEDENCE RULE                                                                                                           SUPPLIED PUBLIC-WIDTH POLICY\n\n\n      Annotated floor plans control physical clearance.                                                                                         Minimum 1,200 mm\n      Visitor-flow workbook evidence controls operational demand and planning comparison. The same rule is applied                              Preferred 1,500 mm\n      to North Loop and South Loop; the sources are not averaged or swapped to favor a route.\n                                                                                                                                                Basis: narrowest point of the public reception approach\n\n\n\n\nCLEANING BOUNDARY - SOURCE RECORDS RETAINED, COMPARISON NORMALISED\n\n\n   Input pattern                                                  Observed in snapshot                                    Treatment                                         Why it matters\n\n  Exact duplicate                                                North workbook width                                     Count once                                        No inflated evidence\n\n\n\n  Case / spacing variants                                        south loop; source labels                                Normalise labels                                  One scheme per route\n\n\n\n  Malformed measurement                                          1,O5 m                                                   Exclude as unusable                               No false precision\n\n\n\n  Staff/loading record                                           Loading spur                                             Exclude                                           Not a public route\n\n\n\n\n    Comparison convention\n    All displayed widths are normalised to millimetres (mm); route lengths are metres (m); flow is visitors per 15 min.\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                             2/7\n\fROUTE ANATOMY\n\n\nNorth Loop | physical conflict at reception approach\n\n\n     ROUTE TOPOLOGY                                                                                                          SOURCE-BACKED WIDTH COMPARISON\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                    Visitor-flow workbook\n                                                                                      RECEPTION APPROACH                       W\n                                                                                                                                    planning comparison\n                                                                                                                                                                                      1,500 mm\n                                                                                            narrow point\n\n\n\n                                                                                                           Reception                Annotated floor plans\n                                                                                           19 m                                 P\n                                                                                                                                    physical control\n                                                                                                                                                                                      1,100 mm\n\n\n                                                                                                                               SOURCE DISAGREEMENT\n                                                                                                                                                                        400 mm difference\n                                    12 m\n\n\n\n             Entry                                    Junction\n                                                                                                                               POLICY STATUS UNDER ANNOTATED-PLAN CONTROL\n\n                                                                                                                               Below minimum by 100 mm - not compliant\n\n     2 turns recorded | 31 m total public route\n\n                                                                                                                               VISITOR FLOW                           ROUTE MEASURE\n             Route = visitor path                 W    W = workbook               P    P = plan                 widths: mm\n                                                                                                                               18 visitors / 15 min                   31 m | 2 turns\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                3/7\n\fROUTE ANATOMY\n\n\nSouth Loop | physical route to reception\n\n\n     ROUTE TOPOLOGY                                                                                                             SOURCE-BACKED WIDTH COMPARISON\n\n\n\n                                                                                        RECEPTION APPROACH\n                                                                                                                                       Visitor-flow workbook\n                                                                                                 narrow point                     W\n                                                                                                                                       planning comparison\n                                                                                                                                                                                         1,250 mm\n                                                                                                    12 m\n\n                                                                                                                Reception\n                                                                                                                                       Annotated floor plans\n                                                                                                                                   P\n                                                                                                                                       physical control\n                                                                                                                                                                                         1,450 mm\n                                                                               Corridor\n\n\n                                        10 m\n                                                                                                                                  SOURCE DISAGREEMENT\n                                                                                                                                                                           200 mm difference\n                             14 m\n\n\n\n            Entry                          Lift lobby                                                                             POLICY STATUS UNDER ANNOTATED-PLAN CONTROL\n\n                                                                                                                                  Minimum met; 50 mm below preferred\n\n     3 turns recorded | 36 m total public route\n\n                                                                                                                                  VISITOR FLOW                           ROUTE MEASURE\n             Route = visitor path                 W   W = workbook                P   P = plan                     widths: mm\n                                                                                                                                  16 visitors / 15 min                   36 m | 3 turns\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                   4/7\n\fONE DECISION VIEW\n\n\nDirect comparison | both routes\n\n   Decision measure                                                         North Loop              South Loop                                        Read-across\n\n\n   Physical clear width (plan control)                                      1,100 mm                1,450 mm                                          South clears minimum\n\n\n\n   Workbook clear width                                                     1,500 mm                1,250 mm                                          Demand source only\n\n\n\n   Source disagreement                                                      400 mm                  200 mm                                            Both conflicts visible\n\n\n\n   Policy status (plan control)                                             Below minimum           Minimum met; below preferred                      Rule applied to both\n\n\n\n   Route length                                                             31 m                    36 m                                              South +5 m\n\n\n\n   Visitor flow                                                             18 / 15 min             16 / 15 min                                       North +2 visitors\n\n\n\n   Turns                                                                    2                       3                                                 South +1 turn\n\n\n\n\n      PHYSICAL WIDTH AGAINST SUPPLIED POLICY (MM)                                       MIN 1,200                                                PREFERRED 1,500\n\n\n\n\n              1000                                                                        1200                       1400                                                      1600\n\n                                                North 1,100\n                                                                                                                                   South 1,450\n                                                                                                                                                                               mm\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                         5/7\n\fDECISION AND CONTROL\n\n\nRecommendation | approve South Loop\n\n\n\n      RECOMMENDED PUBLIC ROUTING\n\n\n      Approve South Loop for public wayfinding                                                                                                                  Plan-first physical clearance rule applied consistently\n\n\n\n\n     WHY THIS ROUTE                                                                                             PRINCIPAL TRADE-OFF\n\n\n     Its annotated-plan width is 1,450 mm, clearing the supplied 1,200 mm minimum. Its                          South Loop is 5 m longer (36 m versus 31 m), adds one turn (3 versus 2), and carries 2 fewer\n     source gap is 200 mm, smaller than North Loop's 400 mm disagreement. Operational                           visitors per 15 min in the workbook observation.\n     demand remains visible at 16 visitors per 15 min.\n\n\n\n\n      NORTH LOOP OUT-OF-RANGE CONDITION AND CONTROL\n\n\n      Junction to Reception: annotated-plan clear width 1,100 mm - 100 mm below minimum; not compliant.\n      Control: keep general visitor wayfinding off this pinch point. Facilities must field-verify the clear width after movable furnishings are cleared and coordinate any correction. Only consider public\n      release after a site check confirms at least 1,200 mm; otherwise retain North Loop for non-public or staff-assisted contingency use.\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                                             6/7\n\fRECORD AND HANDOFF\n\n\nApproval handoff | final completion\n\n\n\n      READ-ONLY SOURCE + CALCULATED COMPARISON                                                                                     USER COMPLETION / EDITABLE\n\n\n      Recommended public routing: South Loop                                                                                       Final sign location\n\n      Precedence: annotated floor plans control physical clear width; visitor-flow workbook controls demand.\n      South Loop: 1,450 mm plan width | 36 m | 16 visitors / 15 min | 3 turns.\n      North Loop: 1,100 mm plan width - below 1,200 mm minimum; do not sign for general arrivals pending verification.\n\n                                                                                                                                   Complete only after the final coordinated location is confirmed.\n\n\n\n\n      COMPACT HANDOFF NOTE\n\n\n      Next user: enter only the final coordinated sign location in the editable field. Verify the facilities snapshot is valid through 30 September 2025 before release. All comparison\n      figures are source-backed or calculated read-only content; do not overwrite or treat them as user inputs.\n\n\n      Snapshot: facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx | Sign location remains unresolved in the source snapshot.\n\n\n\n\nFernhollow Analytics | Elmsworth Clinic | facilities snapshot valid through 30 September 2025                                                                                                         7/7\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a readable PDF with the required filename and extension.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file","grader_hint":"Confirm that the top-level deliverable is named elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf and that a PDF parser can open it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF opens successfully and all pages can be parsed and rendered.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted PDF","grader_hint":"Open with pypdf or an equivalent offline parser and render every page to confirm there is no corrupt page object or missing resource."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF contains exactly seven pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PDF page tree","grader_hint":"Count the pages in the PDF rather than relying on a visible page number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every page uses 16:9 landscape presentation geometry, approximately 13.333 by 7.5 inches.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"MediaBox or CropBox values","grader_hint":"Inspect page boxes and allow a small conversion tolerance for points-to-inches rounding; reject portrait or materially different aspect ratios."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The rendered deck has no material clipping, overlapping text, unreadable labels, or diagram elements extending beyond the page.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered pages","grader_hint":"Review all pages at presentation scale and zoom into tables and diagrams; score only visible production quality, not source-code intent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck identifies the supplied facilities snapshot and its validity date of 30 September 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible provenance text","grader_hint":"Look for the snapshot filename or an unmistakable equivalent together with 30 September 2025 or 2025-09-30."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both routing schemes from the supplied snapshot are clearly named and treated as separate alternatives throughout the comparison.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot and deck","grader_hint":"Match the two normalized scheme labels in the workbook to two distinct headings, diagram labels, and comparison entries in the PDF."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck distinguishes the visitor-flow workbook evidence from the annotated-floor-plan evidence instead of blending them into one unexplained width.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source labels and comparison table","grader_hint":"Verify that each scheme has visibly attributed measurements or observations for both source types."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck states an explicit source-precedence rule for resolving the disagreement.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible decision-basis text","grader_hint":"Accept a clear plan-first, workbook-first, or equivalently explicit bounded interpretation; reject vague wording such as 'sources were considered.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Duplicate or case-variant source entries are not counted as independent evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot rows and deck evidence summary","grader_hint":"Compare the deck's evidence statements against normalized source records and check that duplicated records do not create extra route observations or inflated totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Malformed measurements in the snapshot are excluded or explicitly marked unusable rather than silently converted into precise values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot and methodology/provenance note","grader_hint":"Check the malformed entry in the supplied workbook and ensure the deck either excludes it with a brief explanation or labels it as unusable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Irrelevant non-public or non-route records are not used as evidence for either visitor routing scheme.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot and deck","grader_hint":"Verify that the irrelevant staff/loading record does not appear as a route width, route total, or recommendation input."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Widths are normalized into one consistent unit before comparison, with the unit visibly identified.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Width table and diagrams","grader_hint":"Confirm that metre and millimetre source forms are converted consistently and that every displayed width carries a clear unit or inherits one unambiguously from a labelled table."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The North Loop or equivalent first scheme shows both its workbook width and its annotated-plan width from the cleaned source records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot and deck","grader_hint":"Match the two displayed values to the normalized records for the first scheme; do not require a particular visual layout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The South Loop or equivalent second scheme shows both its workbook width and its annotated-plan width from the cleaned source records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot and deck","grader_hint":"Match the two displayed values to the normalized records for the second scheme."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The disagreement between source measurements is visible for each scheme rather than being hidden behind a single selected number.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison table or paired visual","grader_hint":"Look for paired source values, a delta, or an equivalent explicit conflict marker for both schemes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The supplied minimum and preferred clear-width thresholds are represented accurately and their units are stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot policy text and deck","grader_hint":"Compare the threshold values and meanings to the policy sheet in the snapshot; accept either a table or a clearly labelled visual scale."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The difference between the two source widths for the first scheme is calculated or displayed consistently with the normalized source values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source values and derived comparison","grader_hint":"Recalculate the absolute difference from the two cleaned source values and allow ±1 mm or the equivalent displayed precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The difference between the two source widths for the second scheme is calculated or displayed consistently with the normalized source values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source values and derived comparison","grader_hint":"Recalculate the absolute difference and allow ±1 mm or the equivalent displayed precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each scheme's policy status follows from the selected width interpretation and the supplied minimum/preferred thresholds.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Policy thresholds, source values, and deck status labels","grader_hint":"Check that labels such as below minimum, acceptable, or preferred are not contradicted by the chosen source value and policy threshold."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The displayed route length for each scheme equals the sum of its supplied route-segment lengths.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot route segments and deck comparison","grader_hint":"Sum the segments for each scheme and allow ±0.1 m or the deck's stated rounding precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The first-scheme diagram preserves the supplied route topology and labels its reception approach or narrow point.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot route records and rendered diagram","grader_hint":"Confirm that the named nodes and their order are recognizable and that the width conflict is attached to the relevant approach segment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The second-scheme diagram preserves the supplied route topology and labels its reception approach or narrow point.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot route records and rendered diagram","grader_hint":"Confirm that the second route's supplied nodes and sequence are recognizable and not accidentally copied from the first."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The diagrams include a legend or other direct key for route lines, source marks, and width units.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered diagrams","grader_hint":"A reader should be able to identify the route, the disputed measurement, and the unit without relying on external explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck provides a readable side-by-side or otherwise direct visual comparison of the two schemes across width, route length, and visitor-flow evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison page or pages","grader_hint":"Judge whether a senior reader can compare the alternatives without hunting across unrelated pages; credit tables, charts, or coordinated visuals that achieve this."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck recommends exactly one of the two routing schemes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible recommendation statement","grader_hint":"Accept a single unambiguous recommendation naming one scheme; reject 'either,' 'both,' or an unresolved list of options."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation is consistent with the stated precedence rule and cites at least two relevant comparison facts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation, rule, and comparison evidence","grader_hint":"Trace the recommendation to the chosen source interpretation and to at least two facts such as width status, route length, or flow."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck acknowledges the principal trade-off or downside of the recommended scheme.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation rationale","grader_hint":"Credit a concise, specific downside tied to the source evidence; generic statements such as 'there are risks' do not qualify."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The selected precedence rule is applied consistently to both schemes rather than changing source authority to favor the recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rule statement and both scheme analyses","grader_hint":"Inspect the status and decision-basis treatment for both alternatives; the same stated principle must govern both."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The out-of-range clear width is explicitly identified, with its affected scheme or route segment named.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Width analysis and diagram annotation","grader_hint":"The deck must identify the below-range condition as a condition, not merely show a number that a reader must interpret."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck gives a concrete accommodation or control for the out-of-range condition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mitigation or accommodation callout","grader_hint":"Accept a credible spatial or operational control that addresses passage through the affected segment; reject a vague promise to 'monitor' without an action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accommodation does not relabel the out-of-range width as compliant and preserves the distinction between measured condition and mitigation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Width status and accommodation text","grader_hint":"Check that the underlying width remains marked below the supplied minimum or otherwise out of range even when an accommodation is proposed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accommodation is tied to a verification trigger, operating condition, or responsible follow-up rather than presented as an unsupported permanent fix.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Accommodation callout","grader_hint":"Look for a concrete condition such as confirmation after site coordination, controlled use during peak flow, or a defined follow-up check."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck does not assert a final sign location that is absent from the supplied snapshot.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot sign-location status and rendered deck","grader_hint":"Search visible text, annotations, and form values for an invented location; the unresolved location must remain unresolved."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A clearly labelled completion area contains the exact user-facing label “Final sign location.”","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered completion area","grader_hint":"Accept capitalization and minor typography variation only if the label is unmistakable and not buried in body text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Final sign location area is an editable PDF form field rather than only static text or a decorative line.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"AcroForm field dictionary","grader_hint":"Inspect the field associated with the visible label and confirm it is a text field that is not read-only."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Final sign location form field has no value, default value, placeholder, or example text.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"AcroForm field dictionary and rendered appearance","grader_hint":"Confirm that /V and /DV are absent or empty and that the appearance stream does not contain a placeholder such as TBD, pending, or example."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"User-entry controls are structurally distinguishable from calculated or source-backed fields.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"AcroForm fields and visible labels","grader_hint":"Confirm that the editable completion field is separate from fields or text labelled as source, calculated, derived, or read-only, with no shared field name or ambiguous control."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Calculated comparison fields, if implemented as PDF fields, are read-only and contain values; they are not editable user inputs.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"AcroForm field flags and visible comparison","grader_hint":"Inspect field flags for the derived width differences, policy statuses, or route totals; static non-field text is acceptable for the calculated content, but any such fields must be read-only."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The displayed calculated comparison values agree with the cleaned snapshot values and stated derivations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Snapshot, comparison table, and read-only calculated content","grader_hint":"Recompute width deltas, policy statuses, route totals, and any displayed flow comparison from the supplied records; allow the stated rounding precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The handoff guidance tells the next user what completion information remains to be supplied.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible handoff note","grader_hint":"The note must point the next user to the blank completion field and explain what kind of information belongs there."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The handoff guidance identifies the 30 September 2025 snapshot as the evidence date to verify.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible handoff note","grader_hint":"Accept the date in written or ISO form if it clearly refers to the facilities snapshot."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The handoff guidance warns the next user that the comparison figures are read-only or source-backed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible handoff note and field labels","grader_hint":"Look for a direct instruction not to overwrite or reinterpret the calculated comparison as a user-entry area."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The guidance is compact and subordinate to the decision content rather than crowding out the comparison.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered deck","grader_hint":"Judge whether the handoff note is useful but visually secondary, with the width evidence and recommendation remaining dominant."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A non-specialist senior reader can understand the alternatives, the measurement conflict, the recommendation, and the unresolved sign-location item without external training.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete rendered deck","grader_hint":"Assess plain-language labels, explanatory captions, visible units, and whether the reader can follow the decision without decoding engineering shorthand."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck presents a logical professional narrative from site need and evidence through comparison, decision, accommodation, and handoff.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete rendered deck","grader_hint":"Review the sequence as a senior reviewer would; credit a coherent story even if the visual layout differs from a reference solution."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Dimensions, units, route diagrams, comparison tables, and recommendation callouts agree with one another.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All rendered pages","grader_hint":"Cross-check repeated widths, route names, scheme labels, and unit conventions across every view; no contradictory value may appear in a diagram versus a table."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Leandra is preparing a spatial wayfinding decision artifact for Fernhollow Analytics, using engineering and operational evidence supplied through a frozen facilities snapshot. The audience is a senior decision maker who needs a defensible comparison rather than a technical drawing or raw data extract.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling duplicated, malformed, irrelevant, and inconsistently labelled facilities records.","Choosing and defending one of two plausible source-precedence interpretations.","Comparing physical dimensions and operational flow without hiding the disagreement.","Preserving a genuinely blank interactive completion field while separating it from read-only calculated evidence.","Producing a coherent seven-page decision narrative with diagrams, units, and clean presentation rendering."],"authoring_plan":{"polarity":"blank","structure":{"file":{"type":"PDF","pages":7,"page_geometry":"16:9 landscape, 13.333 x 7.5 inches per page","form":"AcroForm-enabled PDF with one editable unresolved completion field and separate read-only source/calculated fields where useful"},"affordance_schema":{"user_entry":[{"label":"Final sign location","internal_name":"FINAL_SIGN_LOCATION","type":"text","editable":true,"initial_value":"","default_value":"","placeholder":"","must_stay_empty":true}],"source_or_calculated":[{"label":"Workbook width","internal_name":"WORKBOOK_WIDTH","editable":false},{"label":"Annotated plan width","internal_name":"PLAN_WIDTH","editable":false},{"label":"Width difference","internal_name":"WIDTH_DELTA","editable":false},{"label":"Policy status","internal_name":"POLICY_STATUS","editable":false},{"label":"Route length","internal_name":"ROUTE_LENGTH","editable":false}],"separation":"Use distinct visual and structural zones for user-entry completion versus source-backed and derived comparison content. The blank completion field must not share a field name with any calculated field.","guidance":"Include a compact handoff note explaining completion of the blank sign field, verification of the 2025-09-30 snapshot, and the read-only nature of comparison figures."},"content_requirements":{"source_provenance":"Identify the frozen snapshot, date, workbook evidence, annotated-plan evidence, and supplied policy thresholds.","comparison":"Compare both normalized routing schemes on source widths, width discrepancy, policy status, route length, visitor-flow evidence, and route topology.","decision":"State one explicit source-precedence interpretation, apply it to both schemes, recommend one scheme, and disclose the key trade-off.","out_of_range":"Explicitly identify the first scheme's annotated-plan width as below the supplied minimum and provide a concrete accommodation or control with a verification condition.","unresolved_item":"Do not create a sign location. Preserve the source's unresolved status and leave the Final sign location field empty."}},"source_construction":{"filename":"facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx","single_reference_file":true,"workbook_sheets":["Snapshot metadata","Measurements","Route segments","Flow observations","Policy and open items"],"metadata":{"snapshot_valid_date":"2025-09-30","site":"Elmsworth Clinic","purpose":"Frozen facilities evidence for a reception wayfinding decision","source_roles":{"visitor-flow workbook":"operational flow and planning observations","annotated floor plans":"annotated physical observations"}},"clean_measurement_truth":{"width_unit":"mm","minimum_clear_width_mm":1200,"preferred_clear_width_mm":1500,"measurement_basis":"clear width at the narrowest point of the public reception approach","schemes":{"North Loop":{"visitor_flow_per_15_min":18,"workbook_width_mm":1500,"annotated_plan_width_mm":1100,"out_of_range_source":"annotated_plan","route_segments_m":[{"from":"Entry","to":"Junction","length_m":12},{"from":"Junction","to":"Reception","length_m":19}],"turn_count":2},"South Loop":{"visitor_flow_per_15_min":16,"workbook_width_mm":1250,"annotated_plan_width_mm":1450,"route_segments_m":[{"from":"Entry","to":"Lift lobby","length_m":14},{"from":"Lift lobby","to":"Corridor","length_m":10},{"from":"Corridor","to":"Reception","length_m":12}],"turn_count":3}}},"imperfections":["Include an exact duplicate of the North Loop workbook width record.","Include case and whitespace variants of a valid South Loop label.","Include a malformed width string such as 1,O5 m that cannot be safely parsed.","Include an irrelevant staff-loading or non-public route record.","Represent some valid widths in metres and others in millimetres.","Include the same route evidence under slightly inconsistent source labels so normalization is necessary."],"open_item":{"final_sign_location":null,"status":"unresolved pending later coordination","instruction_to_builder":"Do not place a proposed sign location in the source workbook; the deliverable must leave it blank."}},"accepted_decision_readings":[{"precedence":"Annotated floor plans control physical clear width; visitor-flow workbook controls operational demand.","defensible_recommendation":"South Loop, because its annotated physical width is above the supplied minimum while the North Loop contains the below-minimum observed pinch point.","required_disclosure":"The North Loop's 1100 mm condition remains visible and must have an accommodation or control."},{"precedence":"Visitor-flow workbook controls the planning comparison; annotated plans are treated as an observed condition requiring site accommodation.","defensible_recommendation":"North Loop, because its workbook width is preferred and its visitor-flow value is higher, provided the 1100 mm observed condition is explicitly accommodated.","required_disclosure":"The recommendation must not call the 1100 mm plan measurement compliant and must state the condition for proceeding."}],"derived_truth":{"North Loop":{"width_difference_mm":400,"route_length_m":31},"South Loop":{"width_difference_mm":200,"route_length_m":36}},"review_method":"Build a reference PDF offline from the workbook and independently check page count and boxes, AcroForm field flags and values, source-to-output relationships, rendered legibility, narrative coherence, and consistency of all repeated dimensions and units."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"facilities_snapshot_2025_09_30","filename":"facilities_snapshot_2025-09-30.xlsx","purpose":"Frozen external facilities snapshot containing the workbook measurements, annotated-plan measurements, route segments, visitor-flow observations, supplied width policy, and the unresolved sign-location status used to prepare the deck.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this supplied workbook as the sole factual source for the wayfinding comparison; its snapshot date and source labels are recorded inside the file."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"wayfinding_decision_deck","filename":"elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"A revised spatial wayfinding decision deck comparing both routing schemes and presenting a bounded recommendation for senior review.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Produce exactly seven pages in 16:9 landscape presentation geometry.","Use the supplied facilities snapshot as the sole factual source.","Keep the Final sign location user-entry field blank and distinguish user-entry controls from read-only calculated content.","Include source provenance, the selected precedence rule, both scheme comparisons, the out-of-range-width accommodation, and concise handoff guidance.","The PDF must render without clipping, overlap, unreadable labels, or inconsistent units."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"design_artifact","work_product":"presentation_deck","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"artifact_spec@v4","occupation":"producers_directors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"artifact_spec","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Use an independent structural review for PDF internals and a separate domain-oriented visual review for the recommendation narrative and accommodation. Accept either of the two documented precedence readings when it is applied consistently and supported by the snapshot.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["PDF form-field appearance and read-only flags should be checked from the AcroForm dictionary as well as by rendering because viewer behavior varies.","The source supports two bounded precedence interpretations; the grader must not require one fixed recommendation when the chosen rule is explicit and internally consistent."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:25+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:25+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:25+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:23:25+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/04e32c7389f20958","declared_deliverables":["elmsworth_wayfinding_decision_deck.pdf"]};
